**Description**
---------------

### **Build the Future With Us**

Are you passionate about information technology, process improvement, and organizational transformation? Do you want to contribute to a company whose purpose is to help its clients feel confident and secure about their future?




As an IT and Business Process Integration Analyst, you will play a key role in the integration of newly acquired subsidiaries and their alignment with corporate IT processes, systems, and standards. At the intersection of technology and business, you will analyze technology environments, business processes, and IT contracts to support smooth, sustainable integrations aligned with the target corporate operating model.




This permanent full-time position offers an excellent opportunity to showcase your technical, business, and contractual analysis skills while reaching your full potential within a caring and trusted organization. Here, people and their development are at the heart of everything we do, creating an environment that fosters collaboration and innovation.




**What You’ll Accomplish With Us**
----------------------------------

As an **IT and Business Process Integration Analyst**, you will be at the heart of our mission. Your key responsibilities will include:

* Analyze subsidiary technology environments to identify gaps relative to corporate IT standards;
* Document architectures and technical workflows, and assess the impacts of migrations to organizational systems;
* Map existing IT processes and develop transition plans toward the target corporate operating model;
* Gather and structure business requirements, and produce the necessary functional documentation;
* Analyze IT contracts, identify consolidation opportunities, and support technology purchasing decisions;
* Collaborate with IT teams, project managers, and business partners to ensure successful integrations;
* Contribute to risk identification, project governance, and the monitoring of integration activities;
* Support change management initiatives and promote the sustainable adoption of corporate processes and solutions.




**What Could Accelerate Your Success in This Role**
---------------------------------------------------

We are looking for someone who:

* Is recognized for their ability to analyze and simplify complex technological and organizational challenges;
* Excels at connecting business needs with technology solutions;
* Demonstrates a strong ability to map, optimize, and standardize processes;
* Is known for their analytical mindset and ability to provide informed recommendations;
* Possesses a solid understanding of application environments, data, and IT infrastructure;
* Is comfortable collaborating with both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
* Demonstrates strong influencing and communication skills in transformation and change management contexts;
* Has 5 to 10 years of experience in IT analysis, business analysis, or a similar role;
* Has an advanced level of both French and English, as the incumbent will collaborate daily, both verbally and in writing, with unilingual English-speaking partners, teams, and stakeholders across Canada and internationally;




**Why You’ll Love Working With Us**
-----------------------------------

* A work environment where learning and development are combined with a collective pursuit of excellence;
* Artificial intelligence tools available to everyone, helping increase personal efficiency and support organizational growth;
* A healthy, safe, equitable, and inclusive workplace where employees can fully express and develop their potential;
* The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment supported by flexibility and access to inspiring, innovative workspaces.




**Competitive Benefits**
------------------------

* Flexible group insurance plans;
* Competitive pension plan;
* Employee share purchase plan;
* Vacation program and wellness and personal development days;
* Telemedicine services;
* Employee and family assistance program;
* Ergonomic furniture program;
* Performance bonus;
* Discounts on iA products;
* And much more!




**Apply Today and Take the Lead in Your Career**

Where your talent truly matters!




**Not Sure Whether to Apply?**

At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, we encourage you to apply. Your place may be with us, and we would love to get to know you!

**Get ahead of your career, where your talent belongs**
-------------------------------------------------------

See why so many people choose iA!

**Company Overview**
--------------------

iA Financial Group is the strength of a company with a human side, with its over 10,000 employees. Together, we have earned the trust of our more than five million clients and 50,000 advisors who have chosen us for their insurance, savings, and wealth management.

With over $235 billion in assets, we’re a key player in the financial services industry in Canada and the United States. The secret to our success? Investing in you, one person at a time. Because, for over 130 years, we have believed that it’s by supporting our employees and surrounding ourselves with the most reputable leaders in the industry, we will continue to innovate.

At iA, we’re invested in you.

**Our commitment to Diversity and Inclusion**
---------------------------------------------

At iA Financial Group, we support and celebrate diversity. We strive to provide a workplace that is recognized as inclusive for all, regardless of ethnic origin, nationality, language, religious beliefs, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, family situation, or physical o

Macpek est au service de l’industrie du transport depuis plus de 50 ans. Fièrement canadienne et québécoise, notre entreprise est reconnue pour sa capacité à simplifier la vie de nos clients. Nos clients externes regroupent toutes les entreprises œuvrant de près ou de loin dans l’industrie du transport. Quant à nos clients internes, il s’agit de notre équipe, qui s’efforce de faire de Macpek la référence dans notre secteur d’activité.



Notre département des technologies de l’information joue un rôle central dans le succès quotidien et la croissance à long terme de l’entreprise. Il est responsable de fournir des solutions technologiques fiables, sécurisées et efficaces qui soutiennent les opérations d’affaires et permettent à nos équipes de donner le meilleur d’elles‑mêmes.



Se joindre à notre équipe T.I. signifie bien plus que fournir du soutien technique. La personne occupant ce poste participera directement au succès de l’entreprise, en prenant en charge des solutions, en collaborant avec les différents départements et en contribuant à façonner la façon dont la technologie soutient nos activités aujourd’hui et demain.



**Tes missions :**

* Offrir un soutien T.I. fiable et efficace aux utilisateurs :
* + ERP (CSD)
  + B.I. (WhiteCup)
  + Microsoft 365
  + Postes de travail
  + Appareils mobiles;
* Participer à l’optimisation des systèmes et à l’automatisation des processus;
* Assurer la gestion et la maintenance de l’infrastructure technologique;
* Gérer et supporter les solutions de codes à barres RF liées aux opérations et aux inventaires;
* Collaborer avec les équipes internes et les partenaires externes;
* Contribuer à la cybersécurité et à la protection des systèmes et des données;
* Soutenir et améliorer les intégrations EDI avec les fournisseurs;
Améliorer l’expérience utilisateur et la performance des solutions technologiques.  

**Voici ce qui t’attend :**

* Formule magique qui repose sur : passion + respect + équipe + travail = succès assuré;
* Un salaire compétitif, selon ton expérience;
* Assurances collectives afin d’être assuré même pendant ton voyage dans le Sud;
* Régime de retraite pour remplir ton petit cochon rose;
* Remboursement d’activités sportives pour garder ton moteur en pleine forme;
* Rabais pimpants sur les produits, exclusivement pour notre super équipe;
Activités sociales énergisantes et innovatrices.  

Rejoins notre Monde et contribue activement au succès de l’entreprise!

